<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armenia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Armenia is a highland region of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. For centuries it was a contested buffer between rival empires, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucids</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a>, and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and Iranian dynasties. Its control was disputed during the decline of the Seleucid, Sasanian and Afsharid empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armenia.jpg" alt="Armenia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Stepan Malkhasyants Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Armenia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Trade with the Greek cities of the Black Sea, with <b>Armenia</b> and with Iran brought wine, metalwork and luxury goods in exchange for horses, livestock and captives.</blockquote><a href="/empire/alans">Alans · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>After Nicephorus II Phocas retook Cilicia from the Arabs in 965 the Byzantines settled Christians from Syria and <b>Armenia</b> there.</blockquote><a href="/empire/armenian-kingdom-of-cilicia">Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The First Nagorno-Karabakh War with the region's Armenian majority, backed by <b>Armenia</b>, lasted until 1994; both sides committed atrocities and pogroms, among them the Khojaly massacre, the Baku pogrom, the Maraga massacre and the Kirovabad pogrom.</blockquote><a href="/empire/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>A single kingship seems to have formed by the first century BCE, perhaps under the pressure of the wars between Rome, Pontus and <b>Armenia</b> that reached the Caucasus in those decades.</blockquote><a href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Caucasian Albania · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Greece describes special relationships with Cyprus, Italy, France, <b>Armenia</b>, Australia, Israel, the United States and the United Kingdom, belongs to the Council of Europe, the Union for the Mediterranean, NATO and the Francophonie, and joined the Three Seas Initiative in 2023.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hellenic-republic">Hellenic Republic · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In 395 they launched their first large-scale attack on the Eastern Roman Empire, striking Thrace, overrunning <b>Armenia</b>, pillaging Cappadocia and entering Syria, while an invasion of the Sasanian Empire came close to Ctesiphon before a Persian counter-attack defeated it.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hunnic-empire">Hunnic Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
